---
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/legal/LegalDoc.astro';
import { termsVersionLine } from '@client/utils/public/termsVersion';

// The app's old copy in client/src/pages/NutzungsbedingungenPage.tsx is no
// longer served: /app/terms forwards to this page.

const title = 'Terms of Service';
const lastUpdated = termsVersionLine('en');
const description = 'Terms of Service of the Agora Cosmica platform by ChipMates gemeinnützige GmbH. English convenience translation covering scope, AI notices, age requirement, rules of use, liability, and dispute resolution.';
---
<Public
  lang="en"
  title={title}
  fullTitle="Terms of Service | Agora Cosmica"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
  altEn="/terms"
  altDe="/nutzungsbedingungen"
>
  <LegalDoc title={title} lastUpdated={lastUpdated} lang="en">
    <section>
      <p>
        <strong>This English version is a convenience translation. The legally binding version is the German <a href="/nutzungsbedingungen/">Nutzungsbedingungen</a>.</strong>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 1 Scope of Application and Subject Matter of the Contract</h2>
      <p>(1) These Terms of Service apply to the use of the Agora Cosmica platform (hereinafter the "Platform"), operated by ChipMates gemeinnützige GmbH, Schusterstr. 50, 79098 Freiburg im Breisgau (hereinafter the "Provider").</p>
      <p>(2) The Platform offers an AI-powered educational service through which users can get to know historical figures from philosophy, science, art, and activism in text, audio, and images (hereinafter the "Service"). The Provider charges no fee for the Service.</p>
      <p>(3) Deviating or supplementary terms of the user do not become part of the contract.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 2 Description of the Service and Notice on Artificial Intelligence</h2>
      <p>(1) What the figures say in the stories is AI-generated, and so are the voices they speak in. Their portraits are AI-generated images, not photographs.</p>
      <p>(2) AI-generated content can be factually incorrect, incomplete, outdated, or misleading (so-called "hallucinations"). Whether content applies to a specific situation is for the user to check.</p>
      <p>(3) The Service does not constitute professional advice, in particular no medical, psychological, legal, or financial advice. AI-generated content does not replace consultation of qualified professionals.</p>
      <p>(4) The Provider reserves the right to restrict, change, or discontinue the Service in whole or in part at any time. There is no entitlement to uninterrupted availability.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 3 Access and Age Requirement</h2>
      <p>(1) Within the scope of application of the US Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA), use of the Service by persons under 13 is prohibited.</p>
      <p>(2) The Provider reserves the right to restrict access if there are indications that a user does not meet the age requirement in paragraph (1).</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 4 Rules of Use</h2>
      <p>(1) The Service may be used exclusively for private, non-commercial, and educational purposes.</p>
      <p>(2) It is prohibited:</p>
      <p>a) to use the Service for unlawful purposes;</p>
      <p>b) to circumvent, manipulate, or defeat the technical security mechanisms of the Service;</p>
      <p>c) to present or distribute AI-generated content as authentic statements of the historical figures portrayed;</p>
      <p>d) to query the Service in an automated way on a scale that impairs its operation (reading by search engines and other crawlers within the limits of our robots.txt is permitted);</p>
      <p>e) to present AI-generated content as text written by a human or to conceal its AI origin.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 5 Intellectual Property and Rights of Use</h2>
      <p>The Platform's published source code is open source and licensed under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (AGPL-3.0)</a>. The terms of this license govern its use, distribution, and modification. Third-party components in it are subject to their own licenses. The other content of the Platform, in particular its texts, stories, audio recordings, portraits, and graphics, may be protected by copyright or related rights. To the extent such rights exist, they remain with the Provider or the respective rights holders, unless stated otherwise for a particular item.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 6 Data Protection</h2>
      <p>The Provider processes personal data exclusively in accordance with the applicable data protection laws, in particular the GDPR and the BDSG (the German Federal Data Protection Act). For details, please see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 7 Protection of Minors</h2>
      <p>(1) Users and legal guardians can report problematic content by email to <a href="mailto:agoracosmica@chipmates.ai">agoracosmica@chipmates.ai</a>.</p>
      <p>(2) If you are in a crisis or need help, please contact the Telefonseelsorge crisis line (0800 111 0 111, free of charge, 24/7) or the Nummer gegen Kummer helpline (116 111).</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 8 Liability</h2>
      <p>(1) The Provider is liable without limitation for damages arising from injury to life, body, or health that are based on a negligent or intentional breach of duty.</p>
      <p>(2) The Provider is liable without limitation for damages caused by intent or gross negligence.</p>
      <p>(3) In the event of a slightly negligent breach of essential contractual obligations (cardinal obligations), liability is limited to the foreseeable damage typical for this type of contract.</p>
      <p>(4) In all other respects, the Provider's liability for damages caused by slight negligence, in particular for damages arising from the use of or reliance on AI-generated content, is excluded. This applies taking into account that the Provider charges no fee for the Service.</p>
      <p>(5) The above limitations of liability do not apply to claims under the German Product Liability Act or where a guarantee has been given.</p>
      <p>(6) The Provider gives no warranty for the accuracy, completeness, or currency of the AI-generated content. The user uses the content at their own risk.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 9 Blocking and Exclusion</h2>
      <p>(1) The Provider is entitled to block a user's access to the Service temporarily or permanently if the user violates these Terms of Service or misuses the Service.</p>
      <p>(2) In the event of a block due to violations, no prior notice is given.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 10 Changes to the Terms of Service</h2>
      <p>The Provider is entitled to change these Terms of Service with effect for the future, provided this is necessary due to changes in the legal situation, the introduction of new features, the fixing of security vulnerabilities, or other objective reasons, and the user is not unreasonably disadvantaged as a result.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 11 Applicable Law and Dispute Resolution</h2>
      <p>(1) These Terms of Service are governed by the law of the Federal Republic of Germany, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods.</p>
      <p>(2) If the user is a consumer within the meaning of Sect. 13 BGB (the German Civil Code) and has their habitual residence in another country, mandatory consumer protection provisions of that country remain unaffected.</p>
      <p>(3) The Provider is neither willing nor obliged to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a consumer conciliation body.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>§ 12 Contact</h2>
      <p>
        ChipMates gemeinnützige GmbH<br/>
        Schusterstr. 50<br/>
        79098 Freiburg im Breisgau, Germany<br/>
        Email: <a href="mailto:chipmates@chipmates.ai">chipmates@chipmates.ai</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalDoc>
</Public>
